-- A write that creates an entity of a class the writing pack may not create is REFUSED WITH A RECEIPT (#1143, operator 2026-11-14): it used to be dropped silently (a view pack drawing `DomNode:...` with
-- no loaded pack declaring DomNode did nothing, no message). The cases: a write to an EXISTING entity of a class no pack owns stays legal; creating one as an unprivileged pack is the silent case.
-- Converted from tests/loud_1143.rs.

test creating an entity of a class no pack declares is refused with a receipt naming entity class and pack
load draw.c1f
given Trig:t {}
write Trig:t.go = 1
absent Ghost:made
eval 'Ghost:made' in str(Trig:t.refused) = true
eval 'Ghost' in str(Trig:t.refused) = true
eval 'draw' in str(Trig:t.refused) = true
eval 'no loaded pack declares' in str(Trig:t.refused) = true

test creating an entity of another packs class without the import is refused with a receipt
load own.c1f
load draw.c1f
given Trig:t {}
write Trig:t.mk = 1
absent Cls:made
eval 'Cls:made' in str(Trig:t.refused) = true
eval 'draw' in str(Trig:t.refused) = true
eval 'own' in str(Trig:t.refused) = true
eval 'IMPORT own' in str(Trig:t.refused) = true

test legal writes are unchanged
load draw.c1f
given Trig:t {}
given Ghost:old {}
-- an existing entity of a class no pack owns: written, no receipt
write Trig:t.ex = 1
reads Ghost:old.val = 1
reads Trig:t.refused = null
-- the person (outside writer) creates and writes any class
given Ghost:person {}
write Ghost:person.val = 2
reads Ghost:person.val = 2
-- a privileged pack creates a class no pack owns
write Pack:draw.privileged = true
write Trig:t.go = 2
reads Ghost:made.val = 1
